  "name": "development rung, the 125M endpoint row count (T32 / d768 / f1024, 12 heads of 64 over 4 KV heads)",
  "norm_top_limb_is_full_byte": true,
  "note": "LANE STAGE 33 (item 4b of stage 32's heavy-only list): the 125M ENDPOINT ROW COUNT at a ten-log endpoint. The external endpoint commits the padded Dom::D cube, t_pad * d_pad, in rows of 2^endpoint_log_n; at 125M that is 2^19 / 2^14 = 32 data rows and 37 commitment rows, and every other shape has 2, 4 or 16. Here the cube is 32 * 1024 = 2^15 and the endpoint log is the default 10, so the counts are 32 and 37 EXACTLY as at 125M, at a twentieth of the receipt. The head axis, the width 768 and the hidden 1024 are rung-W14's and 125M's, so D_max is 908,065, norm_wrho is 32 and correction C-6 applies; f_e = 12 at 32 tokens gives wrho_s = 17 and three sigma_s limbs, as at rung-C6. What it does NOT reach is the endpoint LOG (10 against 125M's 14) and therefore the endpoint's row WIDTH and Merkle depth \u2014 that is rung-W14's half of the same item",
